#!/usr/bin/env bash
# commit-msg — refuse any commit message carrying a Claude session link.
#
# 2026-08-30: a session URL reached a public PR body and 60 commits on
# `main` carried a `Claude-Session:` trailer. The trailer came from an
# assistant-side commit-message convention, so prose telling the assistant
# "don't do that" is the wrong layer — this repo has already measured what
# soft guidance is worth (the 2026-05-22 audit: ~0x firing). The commit
# boundary is where it can be enforced.
#
# Install: git config core.hooksPath .githooks
set -euo pipefail

MSG_FILE="${1:?commit-msg hook requires the message file}"

if grep -Eqi 'claude\.ai/code/session|Claude-Session:|/session_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}' "$MSG_FILE"; then
  cat >&2 <<'MSG'
✗ Commit rejected: the message contains a Claude session link.

Session URLs identify a private assistant transcript and must never reach
commits, PR bodies, code, or documentation (user directive, 2026-08-30).

Remove the `Claude-Session:` trailer / session URL and commit again.
Co-Authored-By trailers are fine — this only blocks session links.
MSG
  exit 1
fi
